BMF header (LE u32):

| offset | value | meaning |
|---|---|---|
| 0x00 | `46 4F 4D 42` | signature = DWORD `0x424D4F46` ("BMOF" stored as "FOMB") |
| 0x04 | `01 00 00 00` | version 1 |
| 0x08 | u32 | compressed size (length of the DS-01 stream) |
| 0x0C | u32 | decompressed size (length of the BMF payload) |

file size = 16 + comp_size.

`bmfdec.c` comment (verbatim): *"BMF file is compressed by DS-01 algorithm with
additional header: 4 bytes 46 4f 4d 42 - 'F' 'O' 'M' 'B'; 4 bytes 01 00 00 00 -
version 0x01; 4 bytes size of compressed data ...; 4 bytes size of decompressed
data ..."*.  The DS-01 stream itself starts with `44 53` (`'D','S'` = LE u16
`0x5344`), then version `00 01`, then the LZ77 bit-stream.

Five BMF buffers were located by byte-scanning `20-acpi/aml/*.aml` for the magic
(AML `Buffer` contents are stored verbatim):

| AML object | file:line | owning device (_HID/_UID) | bytes 0x00-0x0F | comp | decomp |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `WQBD` | DSDT.dsl:15099 | WMI4, PNP0C14, _UID 0x04 | `46 4F 4D 42 01 00 00 00 65 02 00 00 F8 05 00 00` | 0x0265 | 0x05F8 |
| `WQDD` | DSDT.dsl:22186 | GZFD, PNP0C14, _UID "GMZN" | `46 4F 4D 42 01 00 00 00 5D 4D 00 00 C0 FC 01 00` | 0x4D5D | 0x1FCC0 |
| `WQDA` | DSDT.dsl:24944 | WMIU, PNP0C14, _UID "LSK20" | `46 4F 4D 42 01 00 00 00 08 04 00 00 5E 0C 00 00` | 0x0408 | 0x0C5E |
| `WQBA` | SSDT3.dsl:2692 | AOD, PNP0C14, _UID "AOD" | `46 4F 4D 42 01 00 00 00 47 0A 00 00 38 37 00 00` | 0x0A47 | 0x3738 |
| `WQ00` | SSDT6.dsl:4296 | AWMI, PNP0C14, _UID "0x00" | `46 4F 4D 42 01 00 00 00 6D 03 00 00 68 0B 00 00` | 0x036D | 0x0B68 |

All five streams begin `44 53 00 01 1A 7D DA 54 ...`; `WQBD`/`WQDA` additionally
share `... 42 10 05 10 8A ...`.  A shared compressed prefix can only occur for a
deterministic lossless transform of a shared decompressed prefix (the fixed BMF
header plus common string table) -- conclusive evidence of compression, not
encryption.

## 2. Decompressed payload layout (Binary MOF, from `bmfparse.c`)
* `'FOMB'` (0x424D4F46) + u32 `len` = size of first part.
* If `len < filesize`: at offset `len` the 16-byte ASCII marker `BMOFQUALFLAVOR11`,
  u32 `count`, then `count` x (u32 qualifier offset, u32 flavor bits) used to attach
  ToInstance/ToSubclass/DisableOverride/Amended to qualifiers.
* First part = root: u32 `1`, u32 `1`, u32 `nclasses`, then `nclasses` length-prefixed classes.
* Class record: u32, u32 0, u32 qualifiers_len, u32 classdata_len, u32 instance_flag(0),
  qualifiers, classdata, methods.
* `classdata` holds properties `__CLASS`, `__NAMESPACE`, `__SUPERCLASS`, `__CLASSFLAGS`
  and the data variables; every object is length-prefixed and strings are UTF-16LE.
* Variable type byte: low byte = basic type (0x02 SInt16, 0x03 SInt32, 0x04 Real32,
  0x05 Real64, 0x08 String, 0x0B Boolean, 0x10 SInt8, 0x11 UInt8, 0x12 UInt16,
  0x13 UInt32, 0x14 SInt64, 0x15 UInt64, 0x65 Datetime, 0x67 Char16, 0x0D object),
  high byte 0x20 = array; `MAX(n)` qualifier gives the array bound.
* Class -> GUID association is the class qualifier `guid("{...}")`.

